# Commit after changes

**This repo opts out of “only commit when asked.”** After every logical change set, commit before you finish the turn.

A change set = one deployable unit (feature, fix, rule/docs update, or matched code+decision update). Do not batch unrelated prompts into one commit when they were separate user requests.

## End of turn

Before your final reply, if this turn touched files:

1. `git status` — if the tree is dirty with your work, you are not done.
2. `git diff` + `git log -5 --oneline` (match message style).
3. Stage relevant files only (never secrets).
4. Commit with HEREDOC; re-run `git status` (clean for that work).
5. Prefer small focused commits. No amend / force-push / `--no-verify` unless the user asks.

If a sandbox restart is part of verifying the change set, still commit the source (never `.storage` or `dev/config/secrets.yaml`) before finishing the turn.
